  "part": {
    "name": "Spoked sprocket with splined hub insert",
    "description": "A thin, circular, two-solid sprocket or cassette cog. The main solid consists of a toothed outer ring connected by a lightweight sculpted spoke web to a central carrier seat. A separate annular insert provides a fine internal spline interface. STEP dimensions indicate an overall diameter of approximately 113 mm, an axial thickness of 9.525 mm, a volume of 29778.338 mm^3, and 1482 B-rep faces. Compact FACE range notation is used in minor-face lists; ranges are inclusive.",
    "source_views": [
      "front",
      "back",
      "left",
      "right",
      "top",
      "bottom",
      "toprightiso"
    ],
    "symmetry_note": "The part is coaxial about the central bore and has strong approximate rotational periodicity in the outer teeth, spokes, lightening openings, and internal spline. Front and back geometry are not mirror-identical: the front has a visibly sculpted central recess and raised edge bands, while the back has a broader dark annular hub face. The STEP model contains two coaxial solids."
  },
